p.src:
But Locke wants more than the apple case. He wants the stronger land case. If a parcel is tilled, planted, improved, cultivated, and enclosed, then the claim extends beyond the crop to the land itself: $\text{till}+\text{plant}+\text{improve}+\text{cultivate}
\Longrightarrow
\text{property not only in crop but in land}.$

